Currently, nethack permits chaotic characters to obtain holy water through
water prayer.  However, chaotic characters react to holy water by taking
damage -- not something one would think of as happening to something
blessed by eir god.

I propose "aligning" holy water, as follows.

For inventory purposes, water is either holy water, water, or unholy
water.  Holy water is always coaligned holy water and acts as holy water
for blessing items; chaotic characters drinking or being splashed with
holy water react the same as lawful characters (currently) do.

However, water is actually one of seven possible combinations (fixed-width
table ahead):

             lawful         neutral          chaotic
holy      lawful holy     neutral holy     chaotic holy
plain     <----------------plain water-------------->
unholy    lawful unholy   neutral unholy   chaotic unholy

The character's alignment is then applied to the water: each step of
alignment difference moves holy water's effects one step towards unholy
water and unholy water's one step towards holy water.

Water is always blessed or cursed relative to the altar it's blessed at.

This is primarily a bones enhancement; your chaotic wizard's stash of holy
water in a sack will be useless to the lawful samurai who finds his bones,
except as a supply of water, and neutral characters will see a
disproportionate amount of "plain" water.

This has implications for stacking: concievably, one could have three
stacks of water, without having any holy or unholy water.

